-- title:
--   Composite of two Hecke divisor correspondences through the roof level
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $N,\ell,\ell',M$ be nonzero naturals with $M = N\ell\ell'$. All divisor groups are taken on the intermediate fields $\bar F_n :=$ `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull n)`, the $L$-subfield of $L$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of level $n$. Assume: the four degeneracy maps `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` at levels $(N,\ell)$ and $(N,\ell')$ are integral ring homomorphisms ($h\alpha,h\beta,h\alpha',h\beta'$); the property `HasPrincipalDivisors` holds for $\bar F_{N\ell}$, $\bar F_{N\ell'}$ and $\bar F_M$; the roof maps $u =$ `towerInclBar L` for $N\ell \mid M$ and $u' =$ `towerSubstBar L (N*ℓ') ℓ` for $N\ell'\ell \mid M$ are integral ($hu,hu'$); divisibilities $h_1 : N(\ell\ell') \mid M$ and $h_2 : N \mid M$ together with integrality $hs$ of `towerSubstBar L N (ℓ*ℓ')` along $h_1$ and $hi$ of `towerInclBar L` along $h_2$; and the exchange identity `HeckeExchangeAt L N ℓ ℓ' M hM`, namely that for every divisor $D$ on $\bar F_{N\ell'}$ the pullback along `heckeBetaBar L N ℓ` of the pushforward along `heckeAlphaBar L N ℓ'` of $D$ equals the pushforward along $u$ of the pullback along $u'$ of $D$. Then for every divisor $D$ on $\bar F_N$, applying `heckeDivBar hα' hβ'` and then `heckeDivBar hα hβ` (each being pushforward along `heckeAlphaBar` composed after pullback along `heckeBetaBar` at the respective level) gives the same divisor as the single correspondence with pullback leg `towerSubstBar L N (ℓ*ℓ')` and pushforward leg `towerInclBar L h₂`, both into $\bar F_M$.
--
--   This identifies the composite of the divisorial Hecke correspondences at $\ell$ and at $\ell'$ on the modular curve of level $N$ with a single correspondence realised through the roof level $M = N\ell\ell'$, the degeneracy-diagram form of the multiplicativity of Hecke operators. It is used to derive the commutativity of the divisorial Hecke operators `heckeDivBar` at $\ell$ and $\ell'$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_heckeDivBar_heckeDivBar_of_heckeExchangeAt.lean

